{title: Harbor Road}
{artist: Freevia Demo}
{composer: Freevia Demo}
{lyricist: Freevia Demo}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{duration: 210}
{comment: Original demonstration song, created for Freevia. Not a published recording.}

{start_of_intro}
[G] [D] [Em] [C]
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G]Windows glow a[D]long the quay,
[Em]Someone leaves a [C]light for me.
[G]Footsteps find the [D]wooden stair,
[C]Evening gathers [D]in the air.
[G]Fold the map and [D]leave the rain,
[Em]Set your coat be[C]side the flame.
[G]Every mile we [D]walked alone
[C]Brought another [D]story home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_pre_chorus}
[Am]Let the restless [C]water roll,
[G]Let the distant [D]whistle go.
[Am]Here beneath the [C]weathered beams,
[D]There is room for all our dreams.
{end_of_pre_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Carry the [D]light down the [Em]harbor [C]road,
[G]Leave a little [D]space for the [C]hearts we [D]know.
[G]When the night is [D]wide and the [Em]wind blows [C]cold,
[Am]We will find each [D]other on the [G]harbor road.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G]Morning waits be[D]hind the hill,
[Em]Cups are warm and [C]streets are still.
[G]Someone hums a [D]new refrain,
[C]Taps the rhythm [D]on the pane.
[G]Take the words we [D]could not say,
[Em]Turn them into [C]songs today.
[G]Open doors and [D]pull up chairs,
[C]There is more than [D]one voice here.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Carry the [D]light down the [Em]harbor [C]road,
[G]Leave a little [D]space for the [C]hearts we [D]know.
[G]When the night is [D]wide and the [Em]wind blows [C]cold,
[Am]We will find each [D]other on the [G]harbor road.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Em]Not every [C]journey ends in [G]glory,
[Em]Not every [C]traveller knows the [D]way.
[Am]Still we can [C]listen to the [G]story,
[Am]Still we can [C]ask someone to [D]stay.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Carry the [D]light down the [Em]harbor [C]road,
[G]Leave a little [D]space for the [C]hearts we [D]know.
[G]When the night is [D]wide and the [Em]wind blows [C]cold,
[Am]We will find each [D]other on the [G]harbor road.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_outro}
[C]One more voice and [G]one more home,
[Am]No one walks this [D]road a[G]lone.
[G] [D] [C] [G]
{end_of_outro}
